/*
  Label.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0218 · Label (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. The web `components/ui/Label.tsx` resolves exactly
  one key of its own — `t('form.required', 'required')`, the screen-reader suffix appended after the visible
  `*` so a required control's accessible name reads "<label> required" (WCAG 3.3.2 Labels or Instructions).
  That key is mirrored verbatim below. The label's text itself (web `children`) is a caller-supplied,
  already-localized prop, so it owns no key here. The only addition is the native empty-text leaf's
  fallback (the "never a blank box" peer of an empty `<label>`).

  These entries fold into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are kept
  in a per-surface table ("Label") so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings. In test / preview
  bundles `NSLocalizedString` returns the value below, keeping the labels deterministic.
*/

/* --- Mirrored web key (web `t('form.required', 'required')`) --- */

/* Screen-reader suffix appended to a required field's accessible name (WCAG 3.3.2 Labels or Instructions). */
"form.required" = "required";

/* --- Native a11y addition (no web key; the web renders an empty <label>) --- */

/* Fallback shown when the label content is blank, so the surface never renders a bare box. */
"label.empty" = "Unlabeled field";
